invariant: INV-7
file: quic_step.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: the ServerHello step derives the Handshake keys under the
  original version's labels, so a client that switched to version 2
  seals and opens its Handshake packets under version 1's keys while it
  names version 2, and no packet of the server's opens. RFC 9369 section
  4.1 sends every Handshake packet in the negotiated version
  (rfc9369.txt:256-257). test/quic_version_tests.h requires each
  Handshake key after a switch to be the one version 2's labels derive.

--- old
    uint32_t version = q->t.quic_negotiated_version;
    QUIC_KEYS_INIT_SUITE(&q->handshake_rx, version, q->hs.s_hs, q->t.suite);
--- new
    uint32_t version = q->t.cfg.quic_original_version;
    QUIC_KEYS_INIT_SUITE(&q->handshake_rx, version, q->hs.s_hs, q->t.suite);
